    "https://careers.alaska.edu/jobs/instructor-of-accounting-fairbanks-alaska-united-states": {
      "title": "Instructor of Accounting",
      "description": "Instructor of Accounting - Fairbanks, Alaska, United States Skip to main content UA Careers Benefits Search Jobs All Jobs Staff Jobs Faculty Jobs Temporary Jobs Temporary Faculty Jobs Student Jobs Internal Jobs Universities UA Anchorage UA Fairbanks UA Southeast UA System Office Internal Jobs My Profile Kiosk mode Instructor of Accounting Instructor of Accounting 533348 Fairbanks, Alaska, United States Faculty Full-time On Campus UNAC Grade 40 UAF College of Business & Security Are you an experienced accountant or CPA? Do you enjoy sharing your knowledge with others? Please consider applying to teach as a term instructor at the College of Business and Security Management. We have amazing students who are eager to learn, and a team of dedicated and professional faculty and staff to provide support. A successful candidate will have outstanding teaching and communication skills. They will have demonstrated the potential to maintain their academic qualifications through scholarship and professional development, and will actively participate in departmental and university service. Minimum Qualifications: Candidates are required to possess an earned Master of Accountancy or related degree. Candidates should also have practical accounting experience. CPA preferred. Position Details: This position is located on the Troth Yeddha' campus in Fairbanks, starting in the Fall 2027 semester. This is a full-time, non-tenure-track faculty position complete with both a competitive salary and a full employee benefits package . UA provides a generous compensation package that includes retirement options, annual leave, 12 paid holidays per year, tuition waivers for employees and family members, and affordable medical, dental, and vision care coverage. New hires will be placed on the UNAC Faculty Salary Schedule , UNAC Grade 40, based on education and experience. Application review will begin on December 1st, 2026. Applications received by this date will receive pri